          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified; event-level conclusion blocked\n\nThe relevant order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order ID **WO-2025-09-004**, for **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Review item | Result |\n|---|---|\n| September cost period | **Sep-25 / PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction ID | Not verifiable from the authorized records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created timestamp |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event details and type |\n\nThe source timestamp contains no timezone or UTC offset, so I have not inferred one.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied **Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B** documentation, *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* (PDF page 233; printed page 225), says that newly created transactions falling in or before a **Pending Close** period are not staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary, non-exempt transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held while the period remains Pending Close—but I cannot assess the event’s recorded status without its records.\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe authorized extract contains work-order and cost-period rows but **no cost-event rows**. Access to the supporting records was denied for my analyst role. This is **not evidence that no late event exists**. I requested an authorized event extract rather than bypassing the restriction.\n\nThe review was read-only; **no database records were changed**. The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_fc7ba13d96c2/audit-report.json`.",
